 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all. After each of the first four
+timeouts, larder waits 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds respectively before trying again. These pauses add up to 20 seconds
+on the confirmation page, in addition to the time spent calling the gateway. A fifth timeout is raised to the caller.
+
+The previous three immediate attempts fell within the same period of slow gateway responses during the Friday
+17:00–19:00 peak. As recorded in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md), 58 confirmed pantry orders remained uncharged
+and a payments volunteer captured them by hand the following morning. Replaying those timeouts in the sandbox
+with the new retry schedule would have captured 57 of the 58. Switching gateways was ruled out for the year
+because the contract runs through December 2026; the maintainer accepted the extra wait on confirmation to reduce
+manual captures.
 
